The reacting front of benchmarks/front on the machine's GPU, at -O0 and -O2,
on small grids: the cells are the same bits as sequentially (front.test),
each kernel is an SPMD kernel, and the arrays stay on the device for the
steps.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O0 -fopenmp -fdo-loops --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/front/front.m -o %t0
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY FRONT_SIZE=101 FRONT_STEPS=150 FRONT_SUBSTEPS=20 %t0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/front/front.m -o %t2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY FRONT_SIZE=101 FRONT_STEPS=150 FRONT_SUBSTEPS=20 %t2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=16 FRONT_SIZE=256 FRONT_STEPS=100 %t2 2> %t.info | FileCheck %s
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INFO < %t.info
CHECK: Burnt cells: 13329
CHECK-NEXT: Heat: 1.043024135233932e+05
CHECK-NEXT: Fuel: 5.220529923213294e+04
ODD: Burnt cells: 10198
ODD-NEXT: Heat: 2.833095487108859e+04
ODD-NEXT: Fuel: 3.004395167297623e+00
INFO: Launching kernel {{.*}}front.init_{{.*}} in SPMD mode
INFO: Launching kernel {{.*}}front.step_{{.*}} in SPMD mode
INFO-NOT: Generic

After the region's copies to the device, no step copies any array, until the
region copies them back: 258 x 258 cells of 8 bytes and the array's size are
532520 bytes.
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=32 FRONT_SIZE=256 FRONT_STEPS=10 %t2 2> %t.copies > /dev/null
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COPIES < %t.copies
COPIES: Copying data from host to device, {{.*}}Name=T, at {{.*}}front.m:[[REGION:[0-9]+]]:
COPIES: Copying data from host to device, {{.*}}Name=Z0, at {{.*}}front.m:[[REGION]]:
COPIES-NOT: Size=532520
COPIES: Copying data from device to host, {{.*}}Size=532520, {{.*}}front.m:[[REGION]]:
